## Impact
Any actor can lock a large stake in the final block of any epoch and receive proportional rewards for that epoch with zero prior p

articipation and zero protocol activity requirement. The attack is costless beyond the lock deposit itself (which is returned at unlock), repeatable every epoch and scales linearly with stake size. Every honest participant in a sniped epoch has their rewards diluted proportionally to the attacker's injected balance.




## Recommended mitigation steps

Replace the point-in-time snapshot with a time-weighted average balance across the epoch as below -
```js
// Use average of epoch-start and epoch-end balance
uint256 balStart = _balanceOf(account, _epochTimestampEnd(epoch - 1));
uint256 balEnd   = _balanceOf(account, _epochTimestampEnd(epoch));
return (balStart + balEnd) / 2;
```\

